            p Savvas Tjortjoglou has published a 
                a(href='http://savvastjortjoglou.com/nba-shot-sharts.html') tutorial
                |  on how to create a shot chart using Python. I made a couple of minor changes to his code:
                ol
                    li Each NBA player has a player ID number. Rather than hard code LeBron James&apos; player ID number 2544, I set the player ID number as a variable,
                    li Since this shot chart covers LeBron James&apos; rookie season to the current NBA season, I created an array called &quot;seasons&quot; and set the range of seasons from 2003-04 season to the current 2016-17 season.
                    li The NBA splits each players&apos; stats into regular season and post-season statistics. For LeBron James&apos; career shot chart, we need to run the stats for both the regular season and post-season then add them together.
            p
