            p In February 2018, I received the following email from Nike:
            p
            img(src='/images/nike_email.jpg' width='100%')
            p
            | Obviously, I was interested in hearing what they had to say so we set up a call. In the call, Nike explained that they were planning to build a new building at Nike&apos;s headquarters named after LeBron James. They wanted to create a shot chart of LeBron James&apos; shots in a basketball court inside the building. Apparently, they found this page from searching on the Internet for a LeBron James shot chart. By the end of the call, I agreed to help them create a shot chart of LeBron James&apos; shots until the end of the 2017/2018 NBA season with the following shots highlighted:
            ol
                li
                    b 10-29-2003:
                    |  1st NBA Shot Made (25 pts. vs. Sacremento Kings, set NBA record for most points scored by prep to pro player in debut performance).
                li
                    b 3-20-2005:
                    |  1st NBA 50+ point game (56 pts. @ Toronto Raptors).
